&lt;h1&gt;📘 Topic: Business Continuity Planning (BCP)&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain:&lt;/strong&gt; D7 – Security Operations&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #cissp&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🧾 Definition&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-definition&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-definition&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Business Continuity Planning defines how critical business functions continue during and after a disruptive event. It extends beyond IT to include people, processes, communications, and facilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔑 Key Points&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-points&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-points&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BCP starts with a business impact analysis and identification of critical services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recovery objectives such as RTO and RPO guide planning decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuity strategies should cover alternate sites, communications, staffing, and supplier dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Testing, training, and maintenance are essential for effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚠️ CISSP Insight&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-cissp-insight&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-cissp-insight&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP candidates should understand that continuity planning is a business governance activity, not just a technical recovery exercise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparation should focus on protecting essential operations and customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;⚔️ Key Difference / Trap&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-key-difference--trap&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-key-difference--trap&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP vs DRP&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BCP = business-wide continuity of operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DRP = technical restoration of systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plans that are not tested are not reliable&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercises expose gaps and assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🏗️ Example&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-example&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-example&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;A company uses alternate work locations, backup communications, and recovery procedures to continue payroll processing after a major outage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;📚 References&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-references&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-references&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NIST SP 800-34, Contingency Planning Guide for Federal Information Systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ISO 22301, Security and resilience — Business continuity management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ISO/IEC 27001:2022&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🔁 Quick Recall&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;-quick-recall&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#-quick-recall&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BCP = keep business running&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DRP = restore systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
